From 9ba9f2403d5435303726a088bfe84eebacf953de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:17:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rc: Wireless stability switches, a portal secret per router,
 review fixes (102.8 line)

- Tweaks > Wireless stability, three switches, all off: the radio call timeout (the driver's wait
  per radio call, 2000-5000 ms, applied live; the driver's own value is put back before each
  wireless teardown and set again every five minutes); keep devices a node claims (disable_exap);
  ASUS's background-DFS rule, behind its own switch (the RTCONFIG_HND_ROUTER_AX spelling it hid
  behind is corrected).
- Guest Portal secret: the stock value is the same on every router. Each router now makes a random
  one the first time a portal starts, stored encrypted, or uses the admin's own (Tweaks > Guest
  Portal).
- Restart requests sent from inside rc's own handlers were not carried out; the rules engine's
  dnsmasq reload now runs directly.
- acs_cli2 calls are limited to 10 s; the AiMesh channel fit waits for the controller's lock a
  bounded time, and its JSON reader no longer spins on a stray bracket.
- AiMesh sync files are written private, and older ones are closed at boot. Time Machine and
  portal folders are root's own; afp.conf is written fresh, never through a link.
- The watchdog keeps the radio driver's crash helper running and real, and the roaming assistant's
  local socket root-only. networkmap gets no lan_gateway that is not an IPv4 address. usb.c:
  RTCONFIG_SAMBASRV spelling.
Also in these files: services.c publishes the router's encrypted DNS (DHCP option 162) and writes
dhcp-broadcast (the Encrypted DNS and dnsmasq commits); defaults.c adds the rows of the new
settings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
